      "designMd": "---\nname: Kinetic Enterprise\ncolors:\n  surface: '#f7f9fb'\n  surface-dim: '#d8dadc'\n  surface-bright: '#f7f9fb'\n  surface-container-lowest: '#ffffff'\n  surface-container-low: '#f2f4f6'\n  surface-container: '#eceef0'\n  surface-container-high: '#e6e8ea'\n  surface-container-highest: '#e0e3e5'\n  on-surface: '#191c1e'\n  on-surface-variant: '#444651'\n  inverse-surface: '#2d3133'\n  inverse-on-surface: '#eff1f3'\n  outline: '#757682'\n  outline-variant: '#c5c5d3'\n  surface-tint: '#4059aa'\n  primary: '#00236f'\n  on-primary: '#ffffff'\n  primary-container: '#1e3a8a'\n  on-primary-container: '#90a8ff'\n  inverse-primary: '#b6c4ff'\n  secondary: '#505f76'\n  on-secondary: '#ffffff'\n  secondary-container: '#d0e1fb'\n  on-secondary-container: '#54647a'\n  tertiary: '#222a3e'\n  on-tertiary: '#ffffff'\n  tertiary-container: '#384055'\n  on-tertiary-container: '#a4acc5'\n  error: '#ba1a1a'\n  on-error: '#ffffff'\n  error-container: '#ffdad6'\n  on-error-container: '#93000a'\n  primary-fixed: '#dce1ff'\n  primary-fixed-dim: '#b6c4ff'\n  on-primary-fixed: '#00164e'\n  on-primary-fixed-variant: '#264191'\n  secondary-fixed: '#d3e4fe'\n  secondary-fixed-dim: '#b7c8e1'\n  on-secondary-fixed: '#0b1c30'\n  on-secondary-fixed-variant: '#38485d'\n  tertiary-fixed: '#dae2fd'\n  tertiary-fixed-dim: '#bec6e0'\n  on-tertiary-fixed: '#131b2e'\n  on-tertiary-fixed-variant: '#3f465c'\n  background: '#f7f9fb'\n  on-background: '#191c1e'\n  surface-variant: '#e0e3e5'\ntypography:\n  display:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 36px\n    fontWeight: '700'\n    lineHeight: 44px\n    letterSpacing: -0.02em\n  headline-lg:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 28px\n    fontWeight: '600'\n    lineHeight: 36px\n    letterSpacing: -0.01em\n  headline-md:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 20px\n    fontWeight: '600'\n    lineHeight: 28px\n  body-lg:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 16px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 24px\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 14px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 20px\n  body-sm:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 12px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 16px\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 13px\n    fontWeight: '600'\n    lineHeight: 18px\n    letterSpacing: 0.03em\n  data-tabular:\n    fontFamily: Inter\n    fontSize: 14px\n    fontWeight: '400'\n    lineHeight: 20px\nrounded:\n  sm: 0.125rem\n  DEFAULT: 0.25rem\n  md: 0.375rem\n  lg: 0.5rem\n  xl: 0.75rem\n  full: 9999px\nspacing:\n  unit: 4px\n  container-max: 1440px\n  gutter: 24px\n  margin-page: 32px\n  stack-sm: 8px\n  stack-md: 16px\n  stack-lg: 32px\n---\n\n## Brand & Style\nThe design system is engineered for high-density information management and professional CRM workflows. The brand personality is rooted in reliability, efficiency, and clarity, targeting enterprise users who require a focused environment for managing complex customer data and financial transactions.\n\nThe design style is **Minimalist / Corporate Modern**. It prioritizes function over form, utilizing generous whitespace to reduce cognitive load in data-heavy views. The aesthetic is characterized by a \"utilitarian elegance\"\u2014using precise alignment, subtle borders, and a restricted color palette to create a sense of order and institutional trust.\n\n## Colors\nThis design system utilizes a structured palette to reinforce hierarchy and state:\n- **Primary Blue (#1E3A8A):** Reserved for primary actions, active navigation states, and brand touchpoints.\n- **Surface Neutrals (#F8FAFC):** Used for large background areas to provide a clean, \"paper-like\" workspace. \n- **Functional Accents:** Success (Green), Warning (Amber), and Error (Red) are used exclusively for payment statuses and form validation to ensure immediate visual recognition.\n- **Text & Borders:** Uses high-contrast slates for text and soft grays for borders to maintain definition without visual noise.\n\n## Typography\nInter is the sole typeface for the design system, chosen for its exceptional legibility in tabular data and small-scale labels. \n- **Tabular Data:** Use the `data-tabular` style which enables monospaced numbers to ensure columns in financial reports align vertically.\n- **Hierarchy:** Use `label-md` for table headers and section titles to differentiate them from interactive data points.\n- **Mobile:** Headlines scale down to 24px (headline-md) on mobile devices to preserve screen real estate for data tables.\n\n## Layout & Spacing\nThe layout follows a **Fixed-Fluid Hybrid** model. While the sidebar and navigation occupy fixed widths, the primary workspace expands to fill the screen up to a max-width of 1440px to ensure line lengths remain readable.\n\n- **Grid:** A 12-column grid is used for dashboard widgets and multi-column forms.\n- **Spacing Rhythm:** Based on a 4px baseline. Most components use 16px (stack-md) padding to maintain a professional, airy feel.\n- **Responsive:** On tablet, margins reduce to 24px. On mobile, the 12-column grid collapses to a single column, and the sidebar transforms into a bottom-sheet or drawer navigation.\n\n## Elevation & Depth\nDepth in the design system is communicated through **Tonal Layering** and **Low-Contrast Outlines** rather than heavy shadows.\n- **Level 0 (Background):** #F8FAFC - The base canvas.\n- **Level 1 (Cards/Tables):** White (#FFFFFF) with a 1px solid border (#E2E8F0). No shadow.\n- **Level 2 (Popovers/Dropdowns):** White with a subtle, 4% opacity neutral shadow to distinguish transient elements from the page.\n- **Depth Logic:** Higher elevation is reserved for active inputs and floating action menus. Data containers stay \"flat\" to the page to imply permanence and stability.\n\n## Shapes\nThe design system uses a **Soft (0.25rem)** roundedness logic. This creates a modern look that is more approachable than sharp corners but maintains the architectural rigor required for a professional tool.\n- **Buttons & Inputs:** 4px (0.25rem) radius.\n- **Large Cards & Widgets:** 8px (0.5rem) radius.\n- **Badges:** Fully rounded (pill) to distinguish them from interactive buttons.\n\n## Components\n- **Data Tables:** Use a zebra-striping pattern (odd rows at #F8FAFC) for long records. Headers must remain sticky. Status badges for payments should use a subtle background tint with high-contrast text (e.g., Light Green background with Dark Green text).\n- **Multi-step Forms:** Utilize a horizontal stepper at the top of the container. Each step is contained within a white card. Validation errors must appear inline, shifting content downwards rather than overlapping.\n- **File Upload Zones:** A dashed border (#CBD5E1) marks the drop zone. Upon hover, the border changes to the Primary Blue. Provide clear file-size and type constraints below the action button.\n- **Dashboard Widgets:** Each widget should have a standard header containing the title and a \"More\" (ellipsis) action. Use simple line charts or bar graphs with the Primary and Secondary color palette for financial reporting.\n- **Inputs:** Standardize on a 40px height for all input fields and buttons to ensure a consistent horizontal rhythm.",
